The 1,024-token arm is healthy at step 2,000 of 5,208, and the control's image stage has finished cleanly. There is still no accuracy number for any arm.

**Done this wake**
- **1,024-token arm, stage 1 (text pretraining):** 384,000 of 1M documents seen. Train loss fell from 2.17 to 0.81. Held-out loss is 0.611 on 64 rows, with no NaN, so the run has not collapsed. It should end around 2026-11-14 09:00, well before its time limit.
- **Control (256-token chunks), stage 2 (image training):** finished in 19.2 h on 100k rows, exit 0. Final held-out loss is 0.785. Marked closed.
- **Control finetunes (seeds 42 and 43):** both are past step 100 of 437. Held-out loss at step 100 is 0.465 and 0.468.
- **Early-look evals queued:** 4 cells of 300 questions each, judge chained, on documents and on the long-chunk HotpotQA set. Each later arm's step-100 early look will be compared against these, at the same step and seed.
- **Step-100 checkpoints saved:** the finetune keeps only its 2 newest checkpoints, so it would delete step 100 at step 300 (around 00:40). The sibling freeze campaign lost its pairing point this way. I copied the model files to `expQ/longchunk/ft_cml256_s4{2,3}_step100`, and the early-look evals read those copies.
- **Records:** I added this rule to the campaign law and a matching row to the known-issues file. I also filed two complaints about the expmon tool: probe numbers must be typed by hand, and nothing warns when a checkpoint will be rotated away.

**Running now**
- The 1,024-token stage 1 and both control finetunes, which should end around 04:10 and 04:45 on 2026-11-13.
- The 6 control evals that decide the comparison, chained on the finetunes.
- The 4 early-look evals, waiting for a free GPU on the shared partition.

**Next**
- The next wake comes when all 10 evals have left the queue (around 2026-11-13 06:00, 18 h at most). A failure wakes it earlier.
- The 2,048-token arm launches only after the 1,024-token stage 1 ends, and only if budget allows. So far 8.1 of the 38 GPU-days are spent, and the full plan projects to 35.

Nothing needed from you.
